Done. US-008 is implemented.

**What changed**

`lib/actions.ts` — new `getSale(saleId): Promise<ActionResult<Sale>>`. It calls `GET /v1/sales/:saleId` with the session organization's credential, so the tenancy check *is* the request: the service answers 404 (not 403) for a foreign sale and the action propagates it as `code: "not_found"`. That endpoint answers in `createSale`'s shape — decimal strings, `actorRef`, and items **without** `productName` (only the list endpoint joins the catalog) — so it needs its own `ApiSaleDetail`, and names are resolved separately via `GET /v1/products/:id`, falling back to the product id when a lookup fails (a name is cosmetic, an amount is not).

`app/api/invoices/[saleId]/route.tsx` — `parseSale()` is gone along with the ~60 lines that accepted amounts, quantities, totals and staff name from the browser. The handler is now `GET` (idempotent read, nothing left to send) and maps the action's code to a status: 401 / 403 / 404, else 502.

`app/history/page.tsx` — the two POST forms carrying `JSON.stringify(sale)` are now plain `<a href={/api/invoices/${sale.id}}>` links. This also fixes `app/sell/page.tsx:473`, which already linked the route over GET against a handler that only exported POST — the post-sale "download invoice" button was returning 405.

**Tests** — new `app/api/invoices/[saleId]/route.test.ts` (401 without a session, without even asking the service; 404 for another org's sale; PDF built from the service response; a forged `sale` in the body ignored; 502 when the service fails) plus a `getSale` block in `lib/actions.test.ts`.

One deliberate deviation from the letter of the ACs: the route also stopped accepting POST entirely rather than just ignoring the `sale` field, since the GET form is what the sell page already assumed.

**Validation** — `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm test` (163 tests, 13 files) and `npm run build` all pass. The new tests were verified in reverse: flipping `not_found: 404` to `400` fails the foreign-sale case, and replacing the computed `subtotal` with `0` fails both tests that assert amounts come from the service. No visual check — neither the inventory service (3001) nor the app (3000) was running. No new strings, so i18n is unchanged.

